<div class="card mt-8">
  <div class="card__body">
    <h2>Questions</h2>

    <h3>Can I start for free?</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">
      Yes. HelloDeploy is free to use today, and the Free plan is intended for learning and
      small projects.
    </p>

    <h3>Can I connect my own domain?</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">
      Yes. You verify that you own it, an administrator reviews and provisions it, and you add
      the DNS record HelloDeploy gives you.
    </p>

    <h3>Is domain registration included?</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">
      No. HelloDeploy does not sell or register domains. Buy your domain from a registrar and
      connect it.
    </p>

    <h3>Are databases included?</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">
      No. HelloDeploy does not provide managed databases. Applications connect to an external
      database provider through environment variables.
    </p>

    <h3>What happens if my project needs more resources?</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">
      Allowances are currently set per account by an administrator, so ask and they can be
      raised. When paid plans exist, this is where the upgrade path will be.
    </p>

    <h3>Do I need to manage Linux or Nginx myself?</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">
      No. HelloDeploy handles the container build, the application process, and the web routing
      in front of it, so you do not configure those yourself.
    </p>

    <h3>When will paid plans be available?</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">
      There is no date yet. Billing is not built, and the prices above are proposals rather than
      commitments.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
